    28	// OpenCurrent opens the current git worktree with object alternates enabled.
    29	// The caller owns the returned repository and must close it.
    30	//
    31	// A worktree root that will not resolve is an error, not a reason to open the
    32	// current directory. This used to fall back to ".", which is a different
    33	// repository whenever the two disagree, and go-git disagrees with git in exactly
    34	// the cases that made the resolution fail:
